Known test geometry: solid full-height vertical color-2 guide near center/right; background 9, with a color-7 irregular compact motif to its left. A demo had background 4, guide in column 14 (0-based), and large color-5 motif at rows 6–15, cols 6–11. Demo output added a full-height color-8 stripe at col 7 (0-based), leaving motif unchanged except for new stripe overlay. Thus color-8 stripe is parallel to guide, at a location associated with motif, not simply an arbitrary fixed distance from guide.

For task test (20x19), guide is col 13, motif spans rows 9–17 and cols 1–4. Eight submitted hypotheses all rejected:
1. full-height 8 at col 0 while preserving input;
2. 8 at col 5;
3. 8 at col 10;
4. 8 at col 0;
5. 8 at col 8 and shift motif one col right;
6. 8 at col 8 with motif shifted right one col;
7. 8 at col 8 plus shifting motif right one col;
8. same col-8 stripe and shifted motif.
The transcript variation reflected confusion over whether to shift pattern; these attempts were rejected and do NOT establish exact error cell or rule.

